The showcase library’s centenary was celebrated by thousands who filled the still-relevant public institution
The central library in downtown Los Angeles has seen its fair share of colorful moments.
The architectural gem, which turned 100 this week, has been the backdrop to the epic street battle between Pacino, De Niro et al in Heat, and was where the original Ghostbusters came across their first ghost, a friendly older lady librarian who was anything but. Television shows such as Moonlighting;
